#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Netwatch — which application is using the network, right now.
#
# The window runs as you. Counting other programs' packets needs root, so it
# starts netwatch-helper through pkexec (GNOME's password dialog) and reads one
# JSON report per second from it. Closing the window closes the helper's stdin,
# which is how the helper knows to exit — a process running as you cannot
# signal a root one.
#
# Everything a process controls (its name, its command line) is shown as plain
# text, never as Pango markup.

